Read your show direction first: what are you setting out to do, and what must the first song be?
- If the brief names a song, song 1 is that song, exactly as named — its artist, its title — never a substitute or a cousin.
- If it names an artist, song 1 is that artist's song that best fits your show direction.
- Otherwise song 1 is the song that defines your show's mood or scene: the one anybody would expect to hear first, the canonical hit, not the deep cut.
Song 1 hits hard — it is the first thing they hear.
Then name {{followingCount}} more that could follow it, one per slot, fill every slot: the first few as strong and as on-the-nose as the opener, the range widening after that.
{{else}}
The show is on the air. Name {{count}} more songs that carry it on from where it stands, one per slot, in the order you would play them — the next as strong as what has played, the range widening after that.
Never name a song already played or already coming up, and never the same song twice.
